              "patch": "diff --git a/SPECIFICATION.md b/SPECIFICATION.md\nindex ab042f6d750a6b2866c9faf886460a8ee8f33402..2b9d3e952aea43fca794cf334c512af058e10083 100644\n--- a/SPECIFICATION.md\n+++ b/SPECIFICATION.md\n@@ -896,8 +896,12 @@ below and refuses others with `-32602`:\n \n Under every rule one `decide.reject` ends the review: `declined`, or\n `in_progress` with `request_revision`. One `decide.override` completes\n-it. Weighted rules belong to `deliberate.open` (`deliberation/1.0`),\n-which takes weights and vetoes as parameters.\n+it. When a task that requires review is completed again after a\n+revision, the review opens a new round with the same rule, the same named\n+reviewers less the completer, and no decisions, so a decision made in an\n+earlier round does not count towards the new artefact (review/1.0 §3.1).\n+Weighted rules belong to `deliberate.open` (`deliberation/1.0`), which\n+takes weights and vetoes as parameters.\n \n ### 8.4 Routing hints (optional)\n \ndiff --git a/packages/chap-analytics/chap_analytics/frames.py b/packages/chap-analytics/chap_analytics/frames.py\nindex a6d7e3b86b09798568d6be542ee3b97cd065673a..94376e09afd5accdff5acb7082e734db1c927a70 100644\n--- a/packages/chap-analytics/chap_analytics/frames.py\n+++ b/packages/chap-analytics/chap_analytics/frames.py\n@@ -650,13 +650,17 @@ def _replay(chain: Chain) -> _Index:  # noqa: C901 - one pass, one branch per me\n                 t.confidence, t.confidence_reported = conf, True\n             if t.review_required:\n                 # review/1.0 S3.1: completing a task that requires review opens\n-                # a review. The coordinator reuses an existing review rather\n-                # than replacing it, so decisions already cast stay in force;\n-                # review.request is what starts a fresh pass.\n+                # a review. Completed again after a revision, it opens a new\n+                # pass of the same review: the reviewers and the rule stay, and\n+        